<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 14.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 14.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Monday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Tourism Asset	3666.67   1.10</p>
<p> 2   Portman Min	   342.86   2.16</p>
<p> 3   Niugini Min	   223.02   3.10</p>
<p> 4   Countrywide-PP	183.87   1.14</p>
<p> 5   Mayne Nickless	175.28   7.94</p>
<p> 6   Colonial Coml	 123.50   2.26</p>
<p> 7   Adel Bton Cement    122.46   1.69</p>
<p> 8   Herald Rsc	     85.84   0.97</p>
<p> 9   Forrestania Gold     83.87   2.34</p>
<p>10   Westral Forest	 80.07   2.21</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
